source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: help_of(line)
---
Change who can open, edit and copy a board. Only the flags you give change; read the current values with `b show --with sharing`.
It changes sharing, so it needs -y; without it only the dry run is shown. Paid-plan values are not yet tried against the live Holst server.

USAGE
  holst board share <board> [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  board   The board to change

FLAGS
  -w, --workspace ws     Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
      --link right       Who can open the board by its link: none, viewer, commentator or editor; unchanged by default
      --members right    What workspace members can do: none, viewer, commentator, editor or full; unchanged by default
      --copy right       Who can copy the content: viewer, editor or full; unchanged by default
      --delete right     Who can delete objects: editor or full; unchanged by default
      --tools right      Who can use the timer, voting and bring to me: editor or full; unchanged by default
      --lock right       Who can lock and hide the content of a frame: editor or full; unchanged by default
      --template state   The public template link: on or off; unchanged by default
  -y, --yes              Confirm a risky change; without it only the dry run is shown (exit code 77)
  -n, --dry-run          Show what would change; change nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst b share "Roadmap" --link viewer -y
  $ holst b share "Roadmap" --members editor --copy full -y
  $ holst b share "Roadmap" --link none -n

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
